# WTDRV2.KEY - the script of the second proof of the Windows test driver
# (TEST/WTDRV2.C): lists, combo, edit controls, the three key prefixes,
# accelerators, menus, a message box, a busy hold, an Esc typed ahead
# that stops one, an A line's Esc that the program asks for and one it
# does not, the window minimized and opened again, and OEM text.
S INIT
# single-selection list box: arrow, End, Home, type-ahead
K CTRL-L
S LIST0
K DOWN
S LIST1
K END
S LIST4
K HOME DOWN DOWN
K R
S LISTR
# extended selection: Shift extends the selection from its anchor
K CTRL-K
K HOME
S MARK0
K SHIFT-DOWN SHIFT-DOWN
S MARK2
K SHIFT-UP
S MARK1
K END
K SHIFT-UP SHIFT-UP
S MARKC
# combo box
K CTRL-O
S COMBO0
K DOWN
S COMBO1
K UP UP
S COMBO2
# multi-line edit: Shift letters and digits, Enter, OEM text, Ctrl-Home
K CTRL-SHIFT-E
K SHIFT-H I ENTER
T caf‚ ok
K ENTER SHIFT-1
K CTRL-HOME SHIFT-X CEND 9
S EDIT
# password edit
K SHIFT-F2
T abc
K 7
S PASS
# message box answered by key, twice
K F2
S BOX
K Y
S YES
K F2
K TAB ENTER
S NO
# accelerator with Alt, then the menu by F10 and arrows
K ALT-C
S CHECK
K F10 RIGHT DOWN
S MENU
# Busy holds the script until the timer has run
K DOWN ENTER
S BUSY
# an Esc typed ahead behind Ctrl+B finds Busy holding the script
K CTRL-B
P ESC
S STOPPED
# an A line's Esc is typed when Busy asks for it, and stops it too; one
# the program does not ask for is typed as a K line's, Busy over by then
K CTRL-B
A ESC
S ASKED
K CTRL-L
A END
S UNASKED
# the window minimized by its system menu, another program's active
# then, and opened again
K ALT-SPACE N
O
S BACK
# Alt mnemonics through a submenu, then Exit
K ALT-A S D
S DEEP
K ALT-A X
S GONE
